  "concise_summary": "PKD demonstrates that Malebranche's occasionalist epistemology and theory of divine ideas resolves his longstanding solipsism. He reinterprets his 2-3-74 visionary experience as direct perception of God's pre-existent archetypal ideas (as infinite meaning/significance) and argues that Ubik and VALIS anticipate an information-theoretic theology where God acts as hyper-info and negentropy. He synthesizes this with Gnostic thought, mystical bride-bridegroom imagery (Shiva, Krishna, Christ), and Pauline justification doctrine, claiming that 2-3-74 witnessed a transmundane power overcoming the closed mechanical cosmos.",
  "key_claims": [
    "We know the world only as representations based on God's pre-existent archetypal ideas in God's mind, not the objects themselves",
    "The psyche perceives an 'attribute' of infinity defined as infinite meaning or significance, which is the essential content of the 2-3-74 experience",
    "God is hyper-info (information that is what it refers to), and the Logos is living negentropy; Christ/King Felix both refers to and IS Christ",
    "The Plasmate represents negentropy in its true form, first intuited in Ubik and later experienced as VALIS in 2-3-74",
    "Justification is a perturbation in the cosmic order caused by a transmundane power (not closed-system mechanism), in which God aligns the cosmos to a divine template",
    "Paul's doctrine of justification presupposes a Gnostic/Faustian open cosmos rejecting the deterministic Greco-Babylonian mechanistic worldview"
  ],
